# FORGE Agent Guide

This is a FORGE project. PostgreSQL is the only infrastructure - no Redis, Kafka, or service meshes.

## CLI

Use `forge --help` and `forge <command> --help`. Prefer `forge add` and `forge generate` over manual file creation.

## Function Selection

| Need | Use | Why |
|------|-----|-----|
| Read data | Query | Cacheable, subscribable, no side effects |
| Write data | Mutation | Transactional, atomic, triggers reactivity |
| Call external API | Action | Non-transactional, has HTTP client |
| Async work | Job | Retryable, progress tracking, survives restarts |
| Scheduled task | Cron | Time-based, catch-up support, leader-only |
| Multi-step process | Workflow | Durable, suspendable, compensatable |

**Decision:** Read? → Query | Write DB? → Mutation | External call? → Action | Can retry? → Job | On schedule? → Cron | Multiple steps? → Workflow

## Backend Patterns

```rust
// Context access
ctx.db()                         // Database pool
ctx.http()                       // HTTP client (Action/Job/Cron)
ctx.require_user_id()?           // Auth or error
ctx.dispatch_job(name, args)     // Queue job
ctx.start_workflow(name, input)  // Start workflow

// Query
#[forgex::query]                  // Basic
#[forgex::query(cache = "30s")]   // Cached
#[forgex::query(public)]          // No auth

// Mutation - always authenticated, transactional
#[forgex::mutation]
#[forgex::mutation(timeout = 30)]

// Job
#[forgex::job]
#[retry(max_attempts = 3, backoff = "exponential")]
#[priority = "high"]             // background|low|normal|high|critical
#[idempotent]
ctx.progress(50, "message")?;    // Report progress
ctx.heartbeat().await?;          // Keep alive in loops

// Cron
#[forgex::cron("0 * * * *")]      // Hourly
#[timezone = "UTC"]
#[catch_up]                      // Run missed
ctx.log.info("msg", json!({...}));    // Structured logging

// Workflow
#[forgex::workflow]
#[version = 1]
ctx.step("name", || async { ... }).compensate(...).run().await?;
ctx.sleep(Duration::from_secs(3600)).await?;  // Durable sleep
ctx.wait_for_event("name", timeout).await?;   // External trigger
ctx.parallel().step("a", ...).step("b", ...).run().await?;
```

## Frontend (Svelte 5)

```svelte
// CRITICAL: Never destructure $props() at module level
let props: Props = $props();  // Use props.x in closures

// Data fetching
const users = subscribe(getUsers, {});        // Real-time
const data = await query(getUsers, {});       // One-time
await mutate(createUser, { name, email });    // Write

// Job tracking
const job = createJobTracker<Args>('type', apiUrl);
await job.start({ ... });
job.resume(savedId, () => localStorage.removeItem(key));
// Use: $job.status, $job.progress_percent
```

## Testing

```rust
// Unit tests: no DB needed. Integration tests: real DB (no mocking, per sqlx philosophy).
let ctx = TestQueryContext::authenticated(user_id);
let ctx = TestQueryContext::builder()
    .as_user(id).with_role("admin").build();

// HTTP mocking
let ctx = TestActionContext::builder()
    .mock_http_json("https://api.example.com/*", json!({...}))
    .build();
ctx.http().assert_called("https://api.example.com/*");

// Dispatch verification
assert_job_dispatched!(ctx, "job_name");
assert_workflow_started!(ctx, "workflow_name");
```

## Code Quality

| Principle | Practice |
|-----------|----------|
| **Testability** | Inject deps via context. Pure functions. Isolate I/O at edges. |
| **Fail Fast** | Validate at boundaries. `require_user_id()?` not silent `None`. |
| **Locality** | Related code lives together. No scattered features. |
| **Explicit** | No magic. Clear names. Obvious control flow. |
| **Small Functions** | One thing per function. < 30 lines. Extract named helpers. |
| **No Premature Abstraction** | Duplicate until you have 3 cases. Wrong abstraction > duplication. |
| **Design Out Edge Cases** | Uniform logic over special cases. If you need `if` for edge case, redesign. |
| **Observability** | Structured logs via `ctx.log.*`. Export traces/metrics when sensible. Progress in jobs. |

## Anti-Patterns

| Don't | Do |
|-------|-----|
| External API in Mutation | Use Action |
| `tokio::sleep` in Workflow | `ctx.sleep()` (durable) |
| Destructure `$props()` | Keep reference |
| Poll with `query()` loop | Use `subscribe()` |
| Skip `ctx.heartbeat()` | Call in long loops |
| Manual retry logic | `#[retry(...)]` attribute |

## Structure

```
src/
├── main.rs           # ForgeBuilder, registrations
├── schema/           # #[forgex::model] structs
└── functions/        # Queries, mutations, jobs, crons, workflows

frontend/src/
├── lib/forge/        # Generated (forge generate)
└── routes/           # Pages
```

## Workflow

1. Define schema in `src/schema/` with `#[forgex::model]`
2. Create migration: `migrations/XXXX_description.sql`
3. Add functions with `forge add <type> <name>` or manually
4. Register in `main.rs`
5. Run `forge generate` to update TypeScript types
6. Use generated types in frontend
